==English==

===Etymology===
< {{etyl|la}} {{term|circulatus}}, pp. of {{term|circulare||make circular, encircle}}, a later collateral form of {{term|circulari||form a circle (of men) around one's self}} < {{term|circulus||a circle}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|En-us-circulate.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|circulat|ing}}

# to [[move]], or cause something to move, in [[circle]]s or through a [[circuit]]
# to move from [[person]] to person, as at a [[party]]
# to [[spread]] or [[disseminate]]
# to become [[widely]] [[known]]

====Synonyms====
* [[put about]]
* [[spread]]
* [[disseminate]]

